 666:Core/Src/main.c **** /** Scales the sine reference before it reaches the modulator. Owned by the
 667:Core/Src/main.c ****  *  40kHz ISR, which walks it toward reference_target one step per sample --
 668:Core/Src/main.c ****  *  volatile so neither side caches a stale copy. A 32-bit aligned float is
 669:Core/Src/main.c ****  *  written atomically on Cortex-M4, so no reader sees a half-updated value.
